> that playing skill is crucial. IOW, how much is it balanced WRT
> luck and skill, and (in case there's no more or less effective
> strategy) would only very lucky convict games be winnable?
I've played around a bit with it when it was released, and actually
quite liked the added challenge.  Luck is definitely important in the
very beginning (finding food early on) and its importance tends to
decrease afterwards.  Due to low hit points, careful play (or luck) is
still required in mid-game.  Luck doesn't matter much for initial inventory.

The ball and the shirt I consider as interesting challenges to be
addressed, but at least removal of the ball can definitely wait until
you have found a decent weapon and are ready to leave it behind.  The
shirt was a minor inconvenience to me in one or two games (especially
when I forgot not to enter a shop with it visible), but didn't hinder me
too much.  And, as for the tourist, it provides one more slot to enchant
in end-game.

I got as far as the quest.  At that time (March–May 2012) I also made
several convict game-play specific posts to this group (other people
did, too), which you should still find through Google.  Search for
“convict” in this newsgroup…  I'd especially recommend my article
“Convict 0.7 - Experiences and two bugs” from April 27th, 2012.

